  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes, especially when sentiment is neutral or negative.",
    "Adjust forecasts downward if recent history shows persistent mean reversion toward lower levels, particularly with negative sentiment.",
    "Increase downward bias in forecasts when sentiment is consistently negative or shows strong bearish signals.",
    "Apply lag correction: if true outcome is significantly lower than forecast, reduce next period’s forecast by 5–10% to account for delayed market reaction.",
    "When sentiment is positive but forecast is overoptimistic, apply a 3–5% downward adjustment to prevent overcorrection.",
    "If true outcome consistently underperforms forecast in early periods (e.g., first 5–7 days), apply a smoothing filter to reduce volatility in subsequent forecasts."
  ]
